examples.question_text:
Write the coordinates of $A$ and $B$. Each grid square represents $1$ unit. A student writes $B=(4.5,1.5)$. Explain the mistake.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridcolour,xstep=8mm,ystep=8mm] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {1,...,5}{\path (\n,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};\path (0,\n) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\fill[black] (4,2) circle (2pt);
\path (4,2) node[above right] {$A$};
\fill[black] (1.5,4.5) circle (2pt);
\path (1.5,4.5) node[above right] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read down to the horizontal value, then across to the vertical value.

For $A$, read $4$ across and $2$ up: $A=(4,2)$.

For $B$, each coordinate is halfway between two whole numbers. Read $1.5$ across and $4.5$ up: $B=(1.5,4.5)$.

The student wrote the vertical coordinate first. Coordinates are written $(x,y)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{methodblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[gridcolour,xstep=8mm,ystep=8mm] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {1,...,5}{\path (\n,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};\path (0,\n) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[methodblue,dashed] (4,0)--(4,2)--(0,2);
\draw[methodblue,dashed] (1.5,0)--(1.5,4.5)--(0,4.5);
\fill[black] (4,2) circle (2pt);
\path (4,2) node[above right] {$A$};
\fill[black] (1.5,4.5) circle (2pt);
\path (1.5,4.5) node[above right] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

