Which two points have the same horizontal coordinate? Which two have the same vertical coordinate? Give their coordinates and describe their positions.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridcolour,xstep=8mm,ystep=8mm] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {1,...,6}{\path (\n,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};\path (0,\n) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\foreach \x/\y/\l in {3/1/J,3/5/K,6/5/L}{\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (2pt);\path (\x,\y) node[above right] {$\l$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Three corners of a rectangle are $P(2,2)$, $Q(7,2)$ and $R(7,6)$. Find the coordinates of the fourth corner, $S$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,7) node[above] {$y$};
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\draw[black] (2,2)--(7,2)--(7,6)--(2,6)--cycle;
\foreach \x/\y in {2/2,7/2,7/6,2/6}{\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (2pt);}
\path (2,2) node[below] {$P(2,2)$};
\path (7,2) node[below] {$Q(7,2)$};
\path (7,6) node[above] {$R(7,6)$};
\path (2,6) node[above] {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
